    <DataNode elementId="AT2G29090-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G29090-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O81077" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;CYP707A2&lt;/i&gt; was recombinantly expressed in both insect cells using a baculovirus system |CITS:[15064374]| and yeast |CITS:[15044947]|. In the case of the yeast expression system, the enzyme encoded by the gene, a cytochrome P450 oxidoreductase, was shown to catalyze the hydroxylation of (+)-ABA but not its enantiomer (-)-ABA |CITS:[15044947]|. Interestingly, the catalytic activity could not be detected in the insect cell microsomal preparations |CITS:[15064374]|. The authors of this study postulated that the failure to catalyze the reaction might be the result of the instability of the CYP707A2 protein whose spectral analysis only detected the inactive form with the 420-nm Soret absorption peak |CITS:[15064374]|. Several lines of evidence indicate that CYP707A2 also produces |FRAME:CPD-7729 neophaseate| via |FRAME:CPD-7728 9&apos;-hydroxyabscisate| from |FRAME:CPD-693 2-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-abscisate| as an side-product, hence exhibits abscisic acid 9&apos;-hydroxylase activity. First, the amount of |FRAME:CPD-7729 neophaseate| is severely reduced in a &amp;Delta;CYP707a1a3 double mutant which also shows a dramatic reduction of |FRAME:CPD-7725 phaseic acid|. Furthermore, CYP707A2 is inhibited by the P450 inhibitor |FRAME:CPD-7770 uniconazole-P| which prevents both the generation of |FRAME:CPD-7725 phaseic acid| and |FRAME:CPD-7729 neophaseate| but both are not affected by another P450 inhibitor |FRAME:CPD-17687 tebuconazole| which is specific for 14&amp;alpha;-demethylases. Finally, &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays with CYP707A2 heterologously expressed in yeast demonstrated the conversion of |FRAME:CPD-693 2-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-abscisate| to |FRAME:CPD-7729 neophaseate| via |FRAME:CPD-7728 9&apos;-hydroxyabscisate| in addition to its abscisic acid 8&apos;-hydroxylation activity |CITS:[21414645]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G29090-MONOMER" />
