      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;CYP707A1&lt;/i&gt; was recombinantly expressed in both insect cells using a baculovirus system |CITS:[15064374]| and yeast |CITS:[15044947]|. In both cases, the activity of the enzyme was studied using microsomal preparations. The enzyme was shown to catalyze the hydroxylation of (+)-ABA but not its enantiomer (-)-ABA |CITS:[15064374],[15044947]|. The expression of &lt;i&gt;CYP707A1&lt;/i&gt; in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; plants was shown to be stimulated by application of ABA |CITS:[15064374]|. The CYP707A1 protein is an NADPH-dependent P450 oxidoreductase. Mutation of the highly conserved cysteine residue (Cys411Ala) in the motif &apos;PFGNGTHS&lt;b&gt;C&lt;/b&gt;PG&apos; led to the complete abolition of the production of PA |CITS:[15044947]|. &lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt; in the yeast expression system |CITS:[15044947]|, the direct product of the P450 oxidation reaction, 8&apos;-hydroxy-ABA, was not detected; the product of the reaction is phaseic acid, the product of the spontaneous cyclization of 8&apos;-hydroxy-ABA).</Comment>
